 <div class="jp-model-copy jp-reveal"><div class="jp-kicker">04 / Information architecture</div><h2 style="margin:0;color:var(--jp-forest);font:500 clamp(39px,5vw,62px)/1.06 var(--jp-serif);letter-spacing:-.045em">A clear path from <em style="color:var(--jp-leaf)">story</em> to discovery.</h2><p>A portal feels useful when visitors can move naturally between understanding the industry, exploring products, and finding the right organisation to contact. This diagram shows a conceptual structure for organising those areas.</p><div class="jp-model-notes"><div><span>Primary purpose</span><strong>Industry discovery</strong></div><div><span>Content structure</span><strong>Products · Knowledge · Directory</strong></div><div><span>Visitor outcome</span><strong>Learn, explore, enquire</strong></div><div><span>Model type</span><strong>Conceptual information map</strong></div></div></div>
 <div class="jp-diagram jp-reveal jp-delay-1"><div class="jp-diagram-top"><span>Conceptual portal architecture</span><span>JP / 01</span></div><div class="jp-diagram-core">Jute Portal<small>DISCOVERY & INDUSTRY KNOWLEDGE</small></div><div class="jp-connect"><span></span></div><div class="jp-nodes">
