<section class="jp-section"><div class="jp-wrap">
 <div class="jp-section-head jp-reveal"><div><div class="jp-kicker">05 / Design process</div><h2>Thoughtful structure.<br /><em>Useful experience.</em></h2></div><p class="jp-intro">A practical design workflow turns a broad industry topic into an understandable digital experience. These stages outline the approach behind the case-study presentation.</p></div>
 <div class="jp-workflow">
  <article class="jp-step jp-reveal"><span>PHASE 01</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>Identify the audiences, the information they need, and the main story the portal should communicate.</p></article>
  <article class="jp-step jp-reveal jp-delay-1"><span>PHASE 02</span><h3>Organise</h3><p>Group the content into clear sections and establish navigation between products, industry and knowledge.</p></article>
  <article class="jp-step jp-reveal jp-delay-2"><span>PHASE 03</span><h3>Visualise</h3><p>Use typography, colour, imagery and spacing to make the subject approachable and recognisable.</p></article>
  <article class="jp-step jp-reveal jp-delay-3"><span>PHASE 04</span><h3>Refine</h3><p>Review responsive layouts, reading order, contrast, navigation clarity and the overall visual rhythm.</p></article>
